{# 1. Commands or files, one reader, any number of sources in one statement.
   Row: reader (read_csv | read_json | read_text | read_blob),
        sources (list: a command ends with ' |', a file is its path),
        options (text, may be empty). read_csv / read_json over commands carry ', hive_partitioning := false':
        DuckDB reads hive key=value folders from the path text, which for a command is the command itself, so
        'GREETING=hi cat /x' gains a column (and overwrites a real field of that name). Files keep detection.
   jq is a boolean in the first CTE: when on, SQL appends the fixed '| jq -c ''.[]''' to each command (splits an
   array into lines for read_json) and nothing else. Curl is a command like any other. #}
SELECT * FROM {{ reader }}([$src${{ sources | join(sep="$src$, $src$") }}$src$]{{ options }})
